### ============================================================================
### 🚌 COLLEGE BUS ATTENDANCE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM — REST CLIENT SUITE
### VSCode REST Client (humao.rest-client) Comprehensive API Specification
### Conforms Strictly to Section 6.2 Architecture Directive & Anti-Secret Policy
### ============================================================================
###
### HOW TO RUN IN VSCODE:
### 1. Ensure the backend server is running (`npm run server` or `tsx server.ts`).
### 2. Configure variables in your untracked local .env file.
### 3. Click "Send Request" above any block to execute against live endpoints.
###
### ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES UTILIZED (from .env):
### - BREVO_API_KEY, BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL, BREVO_SENDER_NAME
### - CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME, CLOUDINARY_API_KEY, CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET
### - JWT_SECRET, DATABASE_URL, PORT

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@brevoApiUrl = https://api.brevo.com/v3
@cloudinaryApiUrl = https://api.cloudinary.com/v1_1

# Development Test Parameters (Generic placeholders - No secrets)
@adminEmail = admin@college.edu
@studentEmail = student@college.edu
@inchargeEmail = incharge@college.edu
@testRegNumber = 7376222CB101
@testBusId = BUS-01
@defaultPassword = DevelopmentTestPassword123!
@sampleTimestamp = 1730000000

### ============================================================================
### 1. SYSTEM HEALTH & SETUP STATUS
### ============================================================================

### 1.1 Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.2 Auth Setup Status (Determine if initial Admin exists)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/setup-status
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### 2. BREVO TRANSACTIONAL EMAIL ENGINE (Direct Brevo REST API v3)
### ============================================================================

### 2.1 Brevo Direct: Send 6-Digit Cryptographic Registration OTP
POST {{brevoApiUrl}}/smtp/email
api-key: {{$dotenv BREVO_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "sender": {
    "name": "{{$dotenv BREVO_SENDER_NAME}}",
    "email": "{{$dotenv BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL}}"
  },
  "to": [
    {
      "email": "{{studentEmail}}",
      "name": "Student Commuter"
    }
  ],
  "subject": "[849201] Your College Bus Attendance Registration Code",
  "htmlContent": "<div style='font-family:sans-serif;padding:24px;background:#0b0f19;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:8px;'><h2 style='color:#38bdf8;'>🚌 College Bus Attendance Verification</h2><p>Hello Student Commuter,</p><p>Your 6-digit registration verification code is:</p><h1 style='letter-spacing:8px;color:#38bdf8;font-family:monospace;'>849201</h1><p>This code expires in 10 minutes. If you did not initiate this request, disregard this email.</p></div>"
}

###

### 2.2 Brevo Direct: Send Student Boarding Alert (Transit Confirmation)
POST {{brevoApiUrl}}/smtp/email
api-key: {{$dotenv BREVO_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "sender": {
    "name": "{{$dotenv BREVO_SENDER_NAME}}",
    "email": "{{$dotenv BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL}}"
  },
  "to": [
    {
      "email": "{{studentEmail}}",
      "name": "Parent / Student Guardian"
    }
  ],
  "subject": "🚌 Transit Boarding Confirmed: Bus 01 Evening Route",
  "htmlContent": "<div style='font-family:sans-serif;padding:24px;background:#0b0f19;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:8px;'><h2 style='color:#10b981;'>✅ Student Transit Confirmed</h2><p>Student <strong>Student Commuter</strong> (Reg: 7376222CB101) has successfully boarded <strong>Bus 01</strong> at College Campus Ground.</p><p>Timestamp: <strong>16:52 IST</strong> | Status: <strong>VERIFIED_PRESENT</strong></p></div>"
}

###

### 2.3 Brevo Direct: Send Student Absentee Notice (Missed Session Alert)
POST {{brevoApiUrl}}/smtp/email
api-key: {{$dotenv BREVO_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "sender": {
    "name": "{{$dotenv BREVO_SENDER_NAME}}",
    "email": "{{$dotenv BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL}}"
  },
  "to": [
    {
      "email": "{{studentEmail}}",
      "name": "Parent / Student Guardian"
    }
  ],
  "subject": "⚠️ Absentee Notice: Evening Bus Session Unattended",
  "htmlContent": "<div style='font-family:sans-serif;padding:24px;background:#0b0f19;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:8px;'><h2 style='color:#ef4444;'>⚠️ Attendance Notice</h2><p>Student <strong>Student Commuter</strong> (Reg: 7376222CB101) did not verify attendance on <strong>Bus 01</strong> for the Evening Session.</p><p>Session Closed: <strong>16:55 IST</strong> | Mode: <strong>GROUND_GEOFENCE</strong></p></div>"
}

###

### 2.4 Brevo Direct: Send Cryptographic Password Reset Link
POST {{brevoApiUrl}}/smtp/email
api-key: {{$dotenv BREVO_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "sender": {
    "name": "{{$dotenv BREVO_SENDER_NAME}}",
    "email": "{{$dotenv BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL}}"
  },
  "to": [
    {
      "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
      "name": "System Administrator"
    }
  ],
  "subject": "Reset Your Bus Attendance Portal Password",
  "htmlContent": "<div style='font-family:sans-serif;padding:24px;background:#0b0f19;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:8px;'><h2 style='color:#38bdf8;'>🚌 Password Reset Request</h2><p>Click the secure link below to choose a new password. This link is valid for 15 minutes:</p><p><a href='http://localhost:3001/reset-password?token=a1b2c3d4e5f67890a1b2c3d4e5f67890' style='background:#0284c7;color:#fff;padding:10px 20px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;'>Reset Password</a></p></div>"
}

### ============================================================================
### 3. SUPABASE AUTHENTICATION & RBAC LIFECYCLE (ZERO MOCKS)
### ============================================================================

### 3.1 Initial Admin Setup (Executed only when no admin exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/setup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fleet SuperAdmin",
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{defaultPassword}}"
}

###

### 3.2 Admin Authentication & Token Generation
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{defaultPassword}}"
}

### Capture JWT Token from Admin Login
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

###

### 3.3 Student Authentication & Token Generation (Email or Register Number)
# @name studentLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{studentEmail}}",
  "password": "{{defaultPassword}}"
}

### Capture JWT Token from Student Login
@studentToken = {{studentLogin.response.body.token}}

###

### 3.4 In-Charge Authentication & Token Generation
# @name inchargeLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{inchargeEmail}}",
  "password": "{{defaultPassword}}"
}

### Capture JWT Token from Incharge Login
@inchargeToken = {{inchargeLogin.response.body.token}}

###

### 3.5 Authenticated User Profile (Token Verification & RBAC Claim)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 3.6 Public Bus Fleet Discovery for Signup Registration
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/available-buses
Accept: application/json

###

### 3.7 Student Registration — Request 6-Digit Brevo OTP
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "STUDENT",
  "name": "Kavitha R",
  "registerNumber": "7376222CB109",
  "email": "kavitha.student@college.edu",
  "phone": "+919876543210",
  "password": "{{defaultPassword}}",
  "preferredBusId": "BUS-01"
}

###

### 3.8 Bus In-Charge Registration — Request 6-Digit Brevo OTP
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "INCHARGE",
  "name": "Prof. S. Natarajan",
  "email": "natarajan.incharge@college.edu",
  "phone": "+919876543219",
  "password": "{{defaultPassword}}",
  "busNumber": "BUS-02",
  "routeName": "Karur Central Express"
}

###

### 3.9 Registration OTP Verification & Supabase Account Creation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "kavitha.student@college.edu",
  "otp": "123456"
}

###

### 3.10 Password Reset Request (Dispatches Reset Link via Brevo API)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{studentEmail}}"
}

###

### 3.11 Password Reset Submission (Verifies SHA-256 Token & Updates Password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "development_safe_token_hash_reference",
  "newPassword": "NewStrongDevPassword2026!"
}

### ============================================================================
### 4. CLOUDINARY MEDIA PIPELINE & ID CARD STORAGE
### ============================================================================

### 4.1 Backend Direct Upload Signature Generation
# Retrieves timestamp, SHA-1 signature, and cloudName for secure client upload
# @name getCloudinarySignature
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/media/signature
Accept: application/json

### Capture Signature Parameters
@cloudName = {{getCloudinarySignature.response.body.cloudName}}
@apiKey = {{getCloudinarySignature.response.body.apiKey}}
@signature = {{getCloudinarySignature.response.body.signature}}
@timestamp = {{getCloudinarySignature.response.body.timestamp}}
@folder = {{getCloudinarySignature.response.body.folder}}

###

### 4.2 Direct Cloudinary HTTPS Media Upload (Direct to Cloudinary CDN)
# Uses the signed signature payload generated from endpoint 4.1
POST https://api.cloudinary.com/v1_1/{{$dotenv CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME}}/image/upload
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

file=data%3Aimage%2Fpng%3Bbase64%2CiVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk%2BP%2B%2FHgAFhAJ%2FwlseKgAAAABJRU5ErkJggg%3D%3D&folder=bus-attendance%2Fid_cards&api_key={{$dotenv CLOUDINARY_API_KEY}}&timestamp={{sampleTimestamp}}&signature=development_sample_signature_hash

###

### 4.3 Backend Authenticated Media Upload Pipeline
# Server-side upload to Cloudinary with secure HTTPS URL & Public ID return
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/media/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fileDataUri": "data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk+P+/HgAFhAJ/wlseKgAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==",
  "folder": "bus-attendance/id_cards"
}

###

### 4.4 Student ID Card Verification Upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/media/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fileDataUri": "data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk+P+/HgAFhAJ/wlseKgAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==",
  "folder": "bus-attendance/id_cards"
}

### ============================================================================
### 5. ATTENDANCE, GEOFENCING & REAL-TIME TRANSIT SESSIONS
### ============================================================================

### 5.1 Active Session Retrieval (Global / Campus Default Window)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/session
Accept: application/json

###

### 5.2 Active Session Retrieval for Specific Bus Fleet
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/session?busId={{testBusId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 5.3 In-Charge: Start Ground Attendance Session (Assigned Bus Only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/session/start
Authorization: Bearer {{inchargeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionType": "EVENING",
  "attendanceMode": "GROUND",
  "busId": "{{testBusId}}",
  "radiusMeters": 15,
  "maxGpsAccuracyMeters": 50,
  "latitude": 10.9572,
  "longitude": 78.0766,
  "locationName": "Campus Bus Terminal"
}

###

### 5.4 In-Charge: Start Travelling Transit Attendance Session (Transit Verification)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/session/start
Authorization: Bearer {{inchargeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionType": "EVENING",
  "attendanceMode": "TRAVELLING",
  "busId": "{{testBusId}}",
  "radiusMeters": 1000,
  "maxGpsAccuracyMeters": 1500,
  "latitude": 10.9572,
  "longitude": 78.0766,
  "locationName": "Transit Route Stop - Toll Gate"
}

###

### 5.5 Student: Ground Geofence Check-in & GPS Verification
# Verifies presence against campus perimeter (15m radius default)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "latitude": 10.957205,
  "longitude": 78.076610,
  "accuracy": 8.5,
  "capturedAt": 1730000000000,
  "readings": [
    { "latitude": 10.957201, "longitude": 78.076608, "accuracy": 8.0, "timestamp": 1730000000000 },
    { "latitude": 10.957205, "longitude": 78.076610, "accuracy": 8.5, "timestamp": 1730000001000 },
    { "latitude": 10.957208, "longitude": 78.076612, "accuracy": 8.2, "timestamp": 1730000002000 }
  ]
}

###

### 5.6 Student: Travelling Transit Verification (On-Bus Dynamic Check-in)
# Validates student coordinates relative to active moving bus coordinates
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/verify-location
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "latitude": 10.9580,
  "longitude": 78.0780,
  "accuracy": 12.0,
  "capturedAt": 1730000005000,
  "readings": [
    { "latitude": 10.9580, "longitude": 78.0780, "accuracy": 12.0, "timestamp": 1730000005000 }
  ]
}

###

### 5.7 Mobile Zero-Hardware Biometric: Generate Challenge
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/mobile/challenge
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 5.8 Mobile Zero-Hardware Biometric: Register Credential
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/mobile/register-biometric
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credentialId": "cred_safe_test_identifier_2026",
  "rawId": "raw_test_identifier_hex_token",
  "transports": ["internal"]
}

###

### 5.9 Mobile Zero-Hardware Biometric: Retrieve Registered Credential
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/mobile/credential
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 5.10 Student: Query Personal Attendance History
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/student/attendance-history
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 5.11 In-Charge: Conclude Session & Finalize Daily Attendance Report
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/session/end
Authorization: Bearer {{inchargeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionId": "SESSION-CURRENT-BUS-01"
}

### ============================================================================
### 6. ADMIN FLEET MANAGEMENT, GEOFENCE SETTINGS & AUDIT
### ============================================================================

### 6.1 Admin: Retrieve Pending Student Approvals Queue
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 6.2 Admin: Approve Student Registration
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/approvals/STUDENT-SAMPLE-ID/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "busId": "{{testBusId}}"
}

###

### 6.3 Admin: Retrieve Pending In-Charge Approvals Queue
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/incharges/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 6.4 Admin: Retrieve Campus Transit Fleet Roster
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/buses
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 6.5 Admin: Retrieve Geofence & Session Timers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 6.6 Admin: Update Geofence Perimeter & Transit Windows
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": {
    "name": "VSB Engineering College Campus Ground",
    "latitude": 10.9572,
    "longitude": 78.0766,
    "radiusMeters": 15,
    "maxGpsAccuracyMeters": 50
  },
  "morning": {
    "startTime": "07:30",
    "endTime": "08:15",
    "reportTime": "08:20"
  },
  "evening": {
    "startTime": "16:45",
    "endTime": "17:15",
    "reportTime": "17:20"
  },
  "timezone": "Asia/Kolkata",
  "enforceGps": true
}

###

### 6.7 Admin: Query Finalized Daily Reports
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 6.8 Notifications Feed (RBAC-Filtered Alert Broadcasts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Accept: application/json
